I wanted to seek clarification regarding the proposed changes to the Message Details From interface. Below are the modifications that have been suggested: 
```
export interface MessageDetailsFrom {
  /** id of sending force */
  readonly forceId?: ForceData['uniqid']
  /** CSS color shade for this force */
  readonly forceColor: ForceData['color']
  /** role of the individual that wrote the message */
  readonly roleId: Role['roleId']
  /** URL of icon to display for this force */
  iconURL: ForceData['iconURL']
  /** user-name, as typed into Feedback/insights form */
  name?: string
}
```  
Before proceeding with these changes, could you please confirm if my understanding aligns with the intended task?

issues.body:
I just submitted a FeedbackForm, including a "From" value.

```
{
    "details": {
        "channel": "Feedback",
        "from": {
            "force": "Blue",
            "forceColor": "#3dd0ff",
            "forceId": "f-blue",
            "iconURL": "",
            "name": "Mr Ian",
            "roleId": "blue-mtg-1",
            "roleName": "MTG 1"
        },
        "messageType": "Chat",
        "timestamp": "2024-01-23T10:27:10.034Z",
        "turnNumber": 2
    },
    "message": {
        "content": "some game feedback"
    },
    "messageType": "FeedbackMessage"
}
```

Note the `name` field in the `details`. This field is declared in the `MessageDetailsFrom` typoe.  Since this is message of type `FeedbackMessage` we should move `name` to an optional field within the `MessageFeedback`  type definition.  We should update the rest of the code accordingly. Note: we may need to change the api of `postFeedback`.  Hmm, maybe we should build of a `FeedbackMessage` in the `InsightForm` - and just send the message like any other message - rather than via a custom `postFeedback` API.
